The 1920–21 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 33rd season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish Football League]] and the [[Scottish Cup]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1921.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1920-21|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> Celtic ended the league campaign a distant second to fellow Glasgow team Rangers, ten points behind. In the cup, they lost 1-2 to [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Hearts]] in the fourth round (quarter-finals).

